# Text files use LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true — the default of
# Git for Windows, and a setting that also applies to a WSL checkout on that
# machine — rewrites every file to CRLF. gofmt then reports every Go file as
# needing reformatting, a rebase refuses to start because the tree looks dirty,
# and any path-scoped tooling sees a change set of the whole repository. None of
# that has a content difference behind it.
#
# core.autocrlf is per machine and has to be fixed once per person; this file is
# per repository and holds for everyone who clones it.
* text=auto eol=lf
